[Event "Knight School"]
[Opening "Italian Game"]
[Variation "Blackburne Shilling Gambit"]
[ECO "C50"]
[Character "tactical"]
[Risk "medium"]
[EarlyMate "black"]
[Tricks "trap,smothered-mate,pawn-grab"]
[Refutes "1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bc4 Nd4"]
[Themes "development-lead"]

1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bc4 Nd4 { A trap. The knight looks loose and e5 looks free. } 4. Nxd4 { Take the knight, not the
pawn. } ( 4. Nxe5? { Grabs a pawn and walks into the trap. } 4... Qg5 5. Nxf7?? Qxg2 6. Rf1 Qxe4+ 7. Be2 Nf3# )
4... exd4 5. O-O { White is a whole piece up, so there is no need to hurry: castle and develop. } 5... Bc5 6. Bxf7+ { Even better: a pawn falls with check, and the king is dragged into the open. } 6... Kxf7 7. Qh5+ *
